    stage2_compiled_program_returned_array_len_zero_2026-09-20, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4-61127: the doc's exact reduction (scalar returned array) and the struct-array sort fixture were run on the freshest available binaries (tree-built simple-head.exe, the one-merge-behind fresh-seed, even the stale tracked bin/simple.exe) across interpreter, JIT, and LLVM native lanes - ALL GREEN (nothing reproduces; the fix predates even the one-merge-behind binary). The pure-Simple fix is present in-tree (module_lowering.spl:2459 registers __runtime_array__ return shapes for Array|Slice; local_is_runtime_array expr_dispatch.spl:735; registry mir_data.spl:2639) and the Rust compiled lane handles the returned handle correctly (compile_inline_len header load calls.rs:345; strict array recognition runtime_native.c:3140 - a rejected handle yields rt_len = 0, the reported symptom). Added the missing seed-lane coverage: test/fixtures/native_returned_array_len_zero/main.spl (doc's reduction verbatim + exit-code guards 91-94) and test/01_unit/compiler/mir/returned_array_len_zero_native_spec.spl (pins exact stdout + exit 0 on interpreter control, JIT, and LLVM native lanes through the binary under test; before this only returned_struct_array_native_spec covered the bug and it requires an admitted self-hosted compiler + struct elements). Spec GREEN end-to-end 3/3 (SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP=1 needed around native-build or shard admission refuses; SIMPLE_MCDC_MODE=off needed or an MC/DC-on runner injects an unresolvable static_probe; 900s cold-cache budget). Residuals: the pure-Simple self-hosted lane is not executable here (fix in-tree, covered by the existing tip spec in CI); the doc's deferred Slice<SliceRow> regression remains open by design (no safe owned Slice<T> constructor; the doc forbids raw-pointer fakes - the prescan fix already covers Slice shapes); the two unrelated doc observations (unwrap lowering error, get_raw SIGSEGV) were out of scope. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/mir/returned_array_len_zero_native_spec.spl prevention=test/fixtures/native_returned_array_len_zero/main.spl"
    stage2_compiled_program_returned_array_len_zero_2026-09-20, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: doc's reduction + struct-array sort fixture ran green on interpreter, JIT, and LLVM native lanes across three binaries (fix predates even the one-merge-behind seed). The pure-Simple fix is in-tree (module_lowering.spl:2459 __runtime_array__ return shapes; local_is_runtime_array; mir_data.spl:2639 registry) and the Rust compiled lane handles the returned handle correctly (compile_inline_len header load; strict array recognition runtime_native.c:3140). Added the missing seed-lane coverage: fixture native_returned_array_len_zero (doc reduction + exit guards 91-94) and spec returned_array_len_zero_native_spec pinning exact stdout + exit 0 on interpreter control, JIT, and LLVM native through the binary under test (SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP=1 + SIMPLE_MCDC_MODE=off + 900s cold budget documented). Spec green end-to-end 3/3 on the tree-built HEAD binary; 2/3 on the later combined binary with only the spec's own LLVM-lane example environment-sensitive (native-build admission surface differs; seed lanes pass). Residuals: pure-Simple self-hosted lane covered by the existing tip spec in CI; the deferred Slice<SliceRow> regression stays open by design (no safe owned Slice constructor; doc forbids raw-pointer fakes). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/mir/returned_array_len_zero_native_spec.spl prevention=test/fixtures/native_returned_array_len_zero/main.spl"

